// Meshes of blocks, kept on the GPU and drawn into a scene (see
// devices/scene.ent): the stuff of a world of blocks too big to draw
// box by box. A program says which faces of its blocks are seen (those
// next to air, say) for a part of its world, and the device makes them
// a mesh in a slot of its own, once; then draws every slot it has, each
// frame, as long as it is not made again or dropped:
//
//   import window
//   import scene
//   import mesh
//   capacity Pixels 65536
//   system paint() { .. Pixels .. make_atlas(Pixels, 256, 256, 16) }
//   system chunk() {
//     Faces += { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, side: Side.Top, tile: 1, light: 15, hidden: 0, clear: false }
//     set_mesh(0, Faces)
//     Faces = []
//   }
//   system world3d() {
//     begin_scene(..)
//     draw_meshes(96.0, 0x9ec8f0)
//     end_scene()
//   }
//
// A block is a cube a unit wide from its corner (x, y, z) (the scene's
// axes: y up). Its faces are textured with tiles of one picture, the
// atlas: so many tiles a row, square, the first at the top left. Its
// colours are the window's (0xRRGGBB, or 0xAARRGGBB with some alpha);
// a texel of 0x01RRGGBB, or of an alpha below a tenth, is not drawn at
// all (the gaps between leaves, say); one half clear lets what is behind
// show through,
// for faces marked `clear` (water, glass), which are drawn after the
// others. The faces are shaded by their side (the top brightest, as the
// scene's boxes are), by their `light`, 0 to 15, and at each corner by
// how hidden it is (`hidden`: 0 to 3 a corner, two bits each, the first
// corner lowest: the blocks next to the corner that keep light from it,
// as a program works it out with `corners`); then all of them by the
// daylight (`mesh_daylight`); and they fade into the fog colour as far
// as `draw_meshes` says the eye sees.
//
// Implemented with raylib (devices/mesh.c, devices/mesh.link).
import window
import scene

// The sides of a block: where its face looks.
enum Side { East, West, Top, Bottom, South, North }

// The corners of each side's face, as the device makes them, from the
// corner (x, y, z) of the block (0 or 1 on each axis): the order of the
// two bits each has in a face's `hidden`; and which way the side looks.
table corners[Side] {
  x0: i32, y0: i32, z0: i32, x1: i32, y1: i32, z1: i32,
  x2: i32, y2: i32, z2: i32, x3: i32, y3: i32, z3: i32,
  nx: i32, ny: i32, nz: i32
} = [
  East:   { x0: 1, y0: 0, z0: 1, x1: 1, y1: 0, z1: 0, x2: 1, y2: 1, z2: 0, x3: 1, y3: 1, z3: 1, nx: 1, ny: 0, nz: 0 },
  West:   { x0: 0, y0: 0, z0: 0, x1: 0, y1: 0, z1: 1, x2: 0, y2: 1, z2: 1, x3: 0, y3: 1, z3: 0, nx: -1, ny: 0, nz: 0 },
  Top:    { x0: 0, y0: 1, z0: 1, x1: 1, y1: 1, z1: 1, x2: 1, y2: 1, z2: 0, x3: 0, y3: 1, z3: 0, nx: 0, ny: 1, nz: 0 },
  Bottom: { x0: 0, y0: 0, z0: 0, x1: 1, y1: 0, z1: 0, x2: 1, y2: 0, z2: 1, x3: 0, y3: 0, z3: 1, nx: 0, ny: -1, nz: 0 },
  South:  { x0: 0, y0: 0, z0: 1, x1: 1, y1: 0, z1: 1, x2: 1, y2: 1, z2: 1, x3: 0, y3: 1, z3: 1, nx: 0, ny: 0, nz: 1 },
  North:  { x0: 1, y0: 0, z0: 0, x1: 0, y1: 0, z1: 0, x2: 0, y2: 1, z2: 0, x3: 1, y3: 1, z3: 0, nx: 0, ny: 0, nz: -1 }
]

// The faces of a mesh: of which block, which side, which tile of the
// atlas, how lit (0 dark, 15 full), how hidden each corner is (see
// above); `clear` for one that lets what is behind show through.
transient buffer Faces {
  x: i32, y: i32, z: i32, side: Side, tile: i32, light: i32, hidden: i32, clear: bool
} capacity 262144

// The atlas: a picture of `width` by `height` pixels (`Pixels`, see
// devices/window.ent, row under row), `per_row` tiles a row; or one read
// from a file (a PNG, say; one the program declares as an asset may be
// in it). Before the first mesh is drawn.
extern proc make_atlas(them: Pixels, width: i32, height: i32, per_row: i32)
extern proc load_atlas(file: text[126], per_row: i32)

// Mesh `slot` (0 to 4095) made anew of the faces; with none, dropped.
extern proc set_mesh(slot: i32, them: Faces)
extern proc drop_mesh(slot: i32)
extern proc drop_meshes()

// Every mesh in view, between `begin_scene` and `end_scene`: as far as
// `far` from the eye, fading into `fog` (0xRRGGBB) towards it.
extern proc draw_meshes(far: f32, fog: i32)
// How bright the day is, 0 (no light but the stars') to 1 (noon, as
// they are made: the default), and the colour the light has (0xRRGGBB:
// 0xffffff white, a dusk's warmer, a night's bluer).
extern proc mesh_daylight(part: f32, tint: i32)

// Of the last `draw_meshes`: how many meshes it drew, and how many faces.
extern proc meshes_drawn() -> i32
extern proc faces_drawn() -> i32
